---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site.js';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How Haiyun Grain Machine writes, reviews, sources, updates and corrects its engineering and procurement content."
  lede="This policy explains who writes our technical content, how it is checked, how sources are used, and how readers can report an error."
>
  <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    The Knowledge Centre and product pages exist to help professional buyers understand grain
    milling equipment, project scope, specifications and procurement risk. Content is written for
    engineers, mill owners, project developers and technical buyers — not for the general consumer
    market and not as operating instructions for unqualified personnel.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Authorship</h2>
  <p>
    Articles and product descriptions are prepared by the {site.name} technical content team, with
    input from sales engineers, process engineers and quality staff. Pages may carry a byline such
    as “Technical Content Team” or a named role. We do not publish invented author names,
    qualifications or reviewer credentials. Where a page names an individual, the page states that
    person's role and the scope of their review.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Technical review</h2>
  <p>
    Content that makes a technical claim is reviewed against at least one of the following:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>manufacturer drawings, specifications, test records or approved catalogues;</li>
    <li>published standards, reference books or peer-reviewed literature;</li>
    <li>project records from commissioned installations, with customer details removed;</li>
    <li>measurements or observations made by our engineering team.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Review is proportional to risk. A general explainer may receive a desk review; a page that
    states a capacity, extraction rate or electrical requirement is checked against the current
    technical data before publication.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Sources and attribution</h2>
  <p>
    Where a page relies on an external standard, regulation, book or article, we identify the source
    in the text or in a reference list. We prefer primary sources: standards bodies, equipment
    manufacturers, government guidance and peer-reviewed publications. We do not cite a source to
    imply an endorsement that does not exist.
  </p>
  <p>
    Technical figures are described with their assumptions where possible — for example wheat
    moisture, extraction rate, operating hours or voltage. A number without a basis is treated as
    incomplete, not as a specification.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Use of software and AI</h2>
  <p>
    We may use software, translation tools and AI-assisted drafting to prepare or localise content.
    Such tools are aids, not authorities. Technical claims, names, figures, links and compliance
    statements are checked by a human before publication. We do not publish AI-generated citations,
    reviewer names, certificates or test results that cannot be verified.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Accuracy and updates</h2>
  <p>
    Equipment, standards and recommended practice change. We review high-traffic technical pages
    periodically and update them when a specification, regulation or project lesson changes. The
    “Last updated” date records the last substantive review, not a cosmetic edit. Older pages may
    remain online for reference; check the date and confirm current data with our team before
    ordering.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If you find an error, a broken link, an unclear statement or a figure that does not match the
    current specification, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with the page URL
    and the issue. We aim to acknowledge substantive reports within five working days and correct
    confirmed errors promptly. Where a correction changes a specification, we update the page and
    the date rather than silently deleting the old text.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Independence and commercial content</h2>
  <p>
    Product pages describe equipment we manufacture or supply. They are commercial content and are
    labelled as such by their context. We do not publish paid third-party reviews, sponsored
    rankings or affiliate recommendations. Reference projects are described as examples, not as
    universal proof of performance.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Comments and user content</h2>
  <p>
    The site does not currently host public comments or user-generated profiles. If we add them,
    this policy will be updated with moderation, privacy and correction rules before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial questions and corrections: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    Postal address: {site.address.full}. See also our
    <a href="/about/methodology/">methodology page</a> and
    <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
